2026-08-11 DB: added a nullable, indexed `cost_code` text column to `tickets` (lib/db/src/schema/tickets.ts) — deliberately plain text, not a pg enum, per the task's "easily extensible" requirement; validated against the shared taxonomy at the API boundary (ticketRecords.ts) instead of a DB constraint, so DHG can add codes to the one TS module without a migration. `drizzle-kit push` applied cleanly (pure column addition, no interactive prompt); existing rows backfilled to NULL automatically (never guessed).
2026-08-11 openapi.yaml: added `costCode` (nullable string, no enum — the taxonomy lives in code, not the spec) to TicketExtraction/TicketRecord/CreateTicketRecordInput/UpdateTicketRecordInput. Running `pnpm --filter @workspace/api-spec run codegen` surfaced a real, pre-existing tooling bug unrelated to this change: the installed orval (8.23.0) can't parse this workspace's pnpm-catalog "zod" version string ("catalog:") for its zod-version auto-detection, so on 'auto' it silently emitted Zod-4-only syntax (top-level `zod.int()`) that doesn't exist in this workspace's pinned zod@3, breaking `tsc --build` for every integer field in the spec (years, jobs, ticket ids) — not just the new costCode field. Fixed by pinning `override.zod.version: 3` explicitly in lib/api-spec/orval.config.ts; re-ran codegen and confirmed the resulting diff is now only the costCode additions.
2026-08-11 API server: wired `suggestCostCode()` into both ticket-extraction code paths in tickets.ts (the per-vendor layout parsers and the generic label-anchored fallback), passing vendor+description so a confidently-recognized vendor gets a suggested code and everything else stays null. ticketRecords.ts create/update now read/write costCode and validate it against `isKnownCostCode()` at the API boundary, returning 400 "Unknown cost code" for a non-null unrecognized value (null always passes — "needs review"). Updated the real-fixture OCR regression test (ticket-parser-regression.mjs) with the now-expected costCode per fixture (Metro Green and Willow Oak are both landfill vendors -> 05-110); all 3 real ticket/invoice photos still pass end-to-end through actual Tesseract OCR.
